    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG SƠN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ancient Vietnamese site dating to 500 BCE, associated with the Đông Sơn culture; renowned for advanced metallurgical craft and bronze drums, and as a geographic reference point in early Vietnamese history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region in northern Vietnam associated with the Đông Sơn culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Geographic center associated with the Đông Sơn culture in northern Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Sơn is the region in northern Vietnam associated with the Đông Sơn culture dating back to around 500 BCE, renowned for its advanced bronze-casting metallurgy by the indigenous Lạc Việt, producing tools, weapons, and exquisitely crafted bronze drums used in spiritual rituals and communal ceremonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnam region associated with the Đông Sơn culture, known for bronze artifacts and drums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Sơn is a northern Vietnamese region/culture dating to around 500 BCE, known for the Đông Sơn culture, renowned bronze metallurgy (bronze casting, drums) and ritual artifacts, which played a central role in early Vietnamese civilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnam; cradle of the Đông Sơn culture and Bronze Age developments; key region for early Vietnamese state formation and cultural artifacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Sơn is an ancient locality in northern Vietnam associated with the Đông Sơn culture (c. 500 BCE), renowned for advanced bronze-casting, bronze drums, tool and weapon making, and related ritual ceremonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region associated with the Đông Sơn culture; site of distinctive artifacts such as drums and weapons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Sơn is a region in northern Vietnam celebrated as the cradle of the Đông Sơn culture, renowned for advanced bronze-copper metallurgy and exquisite ritual artifacts such as drums, reflecting a sophisticated craft and ceremonial tradition dating to about 500 BCE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THỜI KỲ ĐỒ ĐỒNG ĐỎ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bronze Age Red Bronze period within the Đông Sơn chronology, characterized by numerous bronze artifacts and ceremonial objects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronze Age in Đông Nam Á, beginning around 500 TCN in the Đông Sơn region.&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronze Age period characterized by widespread use of bronze tools and weapons, part of the Đông Sơn chronology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronze Age period in Southeast Asia; associated with the Đông Sơn culture and its metallurgical developments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronze Age period in Đông Nam Á; early copper-bronze metallurgy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LẠC VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient Vietnamese ethnolinguistic group associated with early northern Vietnamese states; part of the Bách Việt grouping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese ethnolinguistic group in the northern region, associated with early state formation and cultures like Văn Lang."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indigenous northern Vietnamese group, one of the components that merged with the Âu Việt to form the Âu Lạc kingdom in 257 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indigenous population of northern Vietnam, noted for advanced copper-bronze metallurgy and rice farming during the era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lạc Việt is an indigenous Vietnamese people who co-founded Âu Lạc with Văn Lang."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lạc Việt denotes the indigenous people of the northern Red River Delta who unite with Âu Việt to form Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese group; part of the Bách Việt historical context and associated with early state formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lạc Việt denotes the indigenous population of the Red River Delta whose culture and craftsmanship contributed to early metallurgy and regional identity in northern Vietnam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580</data>
    </node>
