      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An archaeological culture/site in northern Vietnam, linked with early Bronze Age developments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronze Age archaeological sites in northern Vietnam; associated with the early emergence of bronze tools and weapons in the Đông Nam Á region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phùng Nguyên culture, an early Bronze Age culture in northern Vietnam, known for metalworking and as a precursor to the Đông Sơn bronze age."&lt;SEP&gt;"See Phùng Nguyên above"&lt;SEP&gt;"Neolithic culture in Vietnam associated with early rice agriculture and pottery; part of the regional archaeological timeline."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phùng Nguyên is an archaeological Bronze Age culture/site in northern Indochina; its sites yielded metal artifacts and is tied to the early Bronze Age onset in Southeast Asia."</data>
