    <node id="&quot;ÂU VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient Vietnamese ethnolinguistic group in the northern region; linked with early states such as Văn Lang and Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indigenous group from the China–Vietnam border region; fused with Lạc Việt to establish the Âu Lạc kingdom in 257 BCE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese tribal group in the north; part of early polities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Việt is an ancient Vietnamese people who migrated from southern China and integrated with Văn Lang; part of the ethnogenesis of early Vietnamese states."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Việt refers to the people from southern China who migrated to the Red River Delta and ultimately merged with Lạc Việt to form Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient Vietnamese tribe; part of the northern Vietnam confederations mentioned alongside Văn Lang and Đông Sơn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Âu Việt is a historical Vietnamese group that contributed to the formation of Âu Lạc through unification with the Lạc Việt, representing one of the tribes involved in early state formation in the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c272541ed6794431c00e6ca7ce7f4da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8643f67e9d45af93e4e82b2745d1580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THỤC PHÁN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alias used by An Dương Vương; historically proclaimed as An Dương Vương, linking the two names as the same ruler in different historical narratives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thục Phán is the personal name used for An Dương Vương, ruler of Âu Lạc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thục Phán is the ruler who proclaimed himself An Dương Vương, linking to the An Dương Vương figure in the legends."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thục Phán is the birth name of the ruler later known as An Dương Vương, highlighting the historic/mythic identity and nomenclature associated with the Âu Lạc throne."</data>
