    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILIPPINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Philippines is the archipelago destination of Cham-Pa trade networks by the medieval period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Philippines, a Southeast Asian country that served as a distant trade destination in Cham-Champa networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philippines are referenced as part of the historical backdrop involving Western colonial powers in Southeast Asia, including Spain and France, shaping regional dynamics in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philippines was under Spanish rule and is cited in connection with colonial diplomacy involving Spain and France."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philippines, the archipelago nation including Mindanao and Mindoro, connected to Cham Pa trade networks in the medieval period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc Philippines mở rộng phạm vi thương mại của Cham Pa vào thập niên 1200."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philippines; referenced as part of the broader Southeast Asia colonial context, originally under Spanish rule during this historical period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẾ QUỐC LA MÃ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Roman Empire; according to the Hậu Hán thư, sent the first envoy to China around 166."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đế quốc La Mã (Roman Empire) is referenced as the source of early Western merchants and contacts shaping trade networks that reached Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire; in 166 CE a delegation from the Roman Empire is said to have passed through routes linked to An Nam on its way to China, illustrating distant trade networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire; referenced as part of early Western contact networks reaching Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire is cited as an early Western contact context with An Nam, mentioning merchants from the Roman era."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire, noted here as the origin of early diplomatic contact with China."&lt;SEP&gt;"Roman Empire; cited as part of early Western contact with Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đế quốc La Mã, có phái đoàn sứ bộ đến Trung Hoa vào năm 166 CE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire, referenced in historical sources as sending a delegation to China."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Roman Empire; its delegation reportedly traveled toward Trung Hoa via routes described in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐƯỜNG THÁI TÔNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tang dynasty emperor who implemented administrative reforms in 627 to consolidate control over the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đường Thái Tông (Tang Taizong) was a Tang Dynasty emperor who initiated administrative reforms to consolidate control in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đường Thái Tông, hoàng đế của nhà Đường, tiến hành cải cách hành chính năm 627 nhằm sáp nhập và điều chỉnh quyền lực ở các châu, huyện."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AN NAM ĐÔ HỘ PHỦ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An Nam đô hộ phủ was the administrative domain governing northern Vietnam under Chinese rule, where Abe no Nakamaro served."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Nam đô hộ phủ, the Tang protectorate established to govern Vietnam and other non-Han populations during the period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tang-era administrative unit governing An Nam; later renamed to Trấn Nam đô hộ phủ."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đơn vị hành chính dưới nhà Đường ở biên giới phía bắc Việt Nam, quản lý nhóm cư dân phi-Hán."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tang dynasty’s protectorate in Vietnam, governing An Nam and overseeing local administration (Giao Châu)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TỐNG BÌNH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancient capital of An Nam; located at the site of modern Hanoi; later associated with Đại La and Tĩnh Hải quân."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tống Bình, a key settlement in the northern protectorate region later known as Đại La (and Hanoi)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tống Bình, thủ phủ Bắc Việt Nam, về sau trở thành thành phố Đại La."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital of An Nam; the city identified as Hà Nội in modern times; later renamed Đại La thành by Cao Biền.&lt;SEP&gt;"Capital of An Nam; the city identified as Hà Nội in modern times; renamed Đại La thành by Cao Biền during reforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tống Bình was the capital region in northern Vietnam under Tang rule, later associated with Đại La as the capital's development progressed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369f1880c271bd6eae21c84158803a3</data>
