      <data key="d1">"Alternative name for Hà Nội, the northern capital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historic name for Hà Nội, the political center of the northern realm during various periods of Vietnamese dynastic struggle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Hanoi used as the northern capital (Đông Kinh/Hà Nội) during the period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Hanoi; another historical reference to the city."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Hà Nội used in Vietnamese sources; the capital city in various periods described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Name used for the restored capital of Đại Việt after independence, renamed as Đông Kinh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Kinh is an alternative name for Hà Nội used in historical contexts, referring to the same capital city in different periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Kinh is the historic name referring to Hanoi, used as the capital in various periods including references in 1688."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical name for Hanoi after relocating the capital."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical term for the northern capital area (present-day Hanoi)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Kinh (Hà Nội) was the northern capital and strategic center during the Lê–Mạc conflicts, later identified with Hà Nội."</data>
