    <node id="&quot;HUẾ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historic city in central Vietnam, referenced as the land surrounding the modern Huế area and a geographic focal point in Cham–Đại Việt interactions and royal administration during the Trần era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ancient capital of Vietnam, setting for Bến Ngự where Phan Bội Châu was confined."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historic capital region; location of Phú Xuân and the Kinh thành Huế.&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical city and later imperial capital region adjacent to Indrapura; established as a political center around 1600."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the city associated with Phú Xuân, the Tây Sơn and Nguyễn capital, the political center."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the imperial capital and seat of the Nguyễn dynasty; mentioned as the site related to treaties and Can Vuong movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the modern city that includes Phú Xuân as its historical capital; it represents the Nguyễn southern capital's location."&lt;SEP&gt;"City in central Vietnam; mentioned in relation to Indrapura and broader Vietnamese geography.&lt;SEP&gt;"Historic central Vietnam region; lies within Nhật Nam in some historical mappings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historic city in central Vietnam; referenced in the text as the land around which Champa and Đại Việt borderlands were located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical capital of Vietnam; site of detention for Phan Bội Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the imperial capital of the Nguyễn dynasty and the political center from which anti-French resistance movements and treaties emerged."&lt;SEP&gt;"Present-day city of Huế; historically the capital region associated with Phú Xuân."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hue, the historic capital in central Vietnam; the Nguyễn Hoàng moved the capital to Phú Xuân, which later became the city of Hue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part of Nhật Nam, from Quảng Bình to Huế."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the central Vietnamese city associated with Bến Ngự and the old imperial center."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imperial city in central Vietnam; historic capital and command center in the Lê dynasty era; mentioned as đô thành Huế near Cham domains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phía nam của Nhật Nam; một phần của Nhật Nam từ Quảng Bình đến Huế."&lt;SEP&gt;"The historic capital city in central Vietnam; served as the imperial seat (Phú Xuân) under Tây Sơn rule and later Vietnamese dynasties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Vietnam capital region; location associated with Bến Ngự and anti-colonial activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"City in central Vietnam where uprisings occurred and where Hue public rallies and Việt Minh leadership activities took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"City where the abdication of Bảo Đại is announced three days before the ceremony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historic city/region in central Vietnam; part of Nhật Nam's territorial expanse under Han influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế (Hue) region around which historical exchanges occurred between Champa and Đại Việt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Huế is the imperial capital region where the abdication of the emperor is finalized and public events occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imperial city established around 1600; located near the Cham heartland (Indrapura)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7da10df4c22499f6e1fbebde9e539db2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561d10717f3ff788e1032021a4cf0614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4943e96cb569799b168fc03f9b7f0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01995274690fe1835d7836e3a481a678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ca8856a3c05c7e29106b40dae03794b</data>
    </node>
