    <node id="&quot;COCHINCHINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cochinchina is a historical region in southern Vietnam referenced in Borri's focus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina is a historical region of southern Vietnam, referenced in Borri's focus and Seventeenth-Century Vietnam sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina is the French colonial term for Nam Kỳ, the southern region of Vietnam under French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"French colonial term for the southern Vietnamese region administered as a separate colony, underpinning Nam Kỳ campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical southern region of Vietnam referenced in seventeenth-century studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina was the French colonial name for the southern part of Vietnam, established as a colony during the 19th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical region in southern Vietnam featured in Borri's writings about seventeenth-century Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina, a historical southern region of Vietnam during colonial times."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French colonial designation for the southern region of Vietnam, later administered as Nam Kỳ under French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina refers to the southern region of Vietnam, discussed in Borri's writings and in the Views of Seventeenth-Century Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"French colonial name for the southern region of Vietnam; part of Indochina federation."</data>
