    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BẮC KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beijing, the capital of China; a central hub of political power which influenced Sino-Vietnamese relations and diplomacy during the late 20th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beijing, thủ đô Trung Quốc; đối tác và đối đầu trong quan hệ Việt Nam-Trung Quốc, nơi diễn ra các phản ứng ngoại giao và tranh chấp khu vực."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beijing; the capital of China, referenced in context of Sino-Vietnamese relations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Kỳ (Tonkin) refers to northern Vietnam; part of the Indochina Federation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Kỳ designates the northern Vietnamese region where French campaigns established control during the late 19th century.&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Kỳ refers to the northern part of Vietnam under French protectorate status and the theatre of campaigns in Tonkin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh is the northern region around which the center of An Nam's thriving port and commerce was established."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh is the northern region near the Như Nguyệt defense line used in the Song-Dai Viet conflict."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh is the region around which An Nam's center rests, contributing to An Nam's development as a prosperous transshipment port receiving goods from southern seas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh is the region around which An Nam's central trading hub developed, contributing to its status as a major port area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh province lay near the frontier where Đại Việt defended against Song incursions during the era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Ninh province, site of the Như Nguyệt defense and battles against Song."&lt;SEP&gt;"Khu vực nằm dọc theo sông Như Nguyệt, nơi diễn ra phòng thủ và chiến trường.&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnam region referenced in territorial arrangements during decolonization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnam region where Yen Bai uprising took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnam region where the Yen Bai uprising occurred against French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern Vietnamese province where Việt Minh units attacked Japanese forces during the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern protectorate region under French rule, part of Indochina's colonial arrangement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern region of Vietnam; described as part of the protectorate system in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern region of Vietnam; included in territorial discussions following negotiations with France."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin (northern Vietnam); site of French campaigns including the capture of Hanoi in 1873."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin region in the northern part of Vietnam, site of the Yen Bai uprising and related nationalist movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin region of northern Vietnam; site of the Yen Bai uprising in 1930 led by VNQDĐ."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vùng Bắc Ninh ở miền bắc Việt Nam, được mô tả là khu vực có trung tâm giáo dục thù tạc quan lại và là một trung tâm thương mại vận chuyển hàng hóa cho An Nam thông qua tuyến đường thủy và bộ."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4820a393047d71ddfc9dd25445f040a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHÁP XÂM LƯỢC VIỆT NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"French invasion of Vietnam (1858–1887) initiating widespread campaign and colonial rule, often framed as protection of missionaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pháp xâm lược Việt Nam refers to the French invasion from 1858 to 1885 that triggered major political and military upheavals in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French invasion of Vietnam driven by colonial aims and missionary protection, culminating in seizures of Vietnamese ports and territories."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAM KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cochinchina region in southern Vietnam under French colonial administration during the era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ (Cochinchina) denotes the southern region of Vietnam under French rule; it later becomes the Nam Kỳ lục tỉnh, a core part of the French Indochina administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ (Cochinchina) is the southern region of Vietnam under French control beginning 1862 and the base for the colonial administration in the south."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern Vietnam (Cochin-China) region, described as temporarily under French rule after WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"The southern region (Cochinchina) whose status was reintegrated into Vietnam in 1949 as part of state-building.&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ (Cochinchina) was the southern region of Vietnam that became a French colonial territory following the early campaigns, central to French expansion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ is the Vietnamese term for Cochinchina; it functioned as the broader southern region under colonial control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ refers to southern Vietnam, the region where the uprising occurred."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ refers to the southern region of Vietnam that was the base and battleground of the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern Vietnam; site of the 1940 Nam Kỳ uprising against French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern region of Vietnam; reintegrated into the Vietnamese territory in 1949 to help realize the State of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ is a region in southern Vietnam referenced in the text as the geographic focus of the uprising and related revolutionary activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ is the geographic region in southern Vietnam where the uprising took place, encompassing multiple provinces and districts and serving as the operational theater."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ is the southern region (Cochinchina) where the uprising occurred, providing the geographic setting for revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern region of Vietnam, mentioned in relation to French administrative control during the period.&lt;SEP&gt;"Cochinchina region of southern Vietnam under French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Geographic region in southern Vietnam where the uprising took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ (Cochinchina) region in southern Vietnam; site of the Khởi nghĩa Nam Kỳ uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ (Southern Vietnam) is the geographic region where the uprising occurred and where regional party activities and mobilizations were organized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ, the southern region and former Cochinchina under French colonial administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical southern region of Vietnam where the uprising occurred."&lt;SEP&gt;"Khu vực Cochinchina ở miền Nam Việt Nam, dưới quyền cai trị của Pháp trong giai đoạn 1945–1946."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ is the southern Vietnamese region associated with the Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ refers to the southern region of Vietnam where the uprising Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa took place and where local revolutionary committees operated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern Vietnam (Cochinchina), region where the Nam Ky uprising occurred against French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Southern Vietnam region, also called Cochinchina; site of colonial administration after 19th century expansion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The southern region of Vietnam; reintegrated into the State of Vietnam after legal procedures in 1949."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TONKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historical northern region of Vietnam referenced in seventeenth-century studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin is the northern Vietnamese region conquered by the French, forming part of the Bắc Kỳ and a focus of campaigns as described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historical region in northern Vietnam featured in Baron's writings about seventeenth-century Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin refers to the northern region of Vietnam (Bắc Kỳ) that France extended control over during the colonial period.&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin (Bắc Kỳ) is the northern region of Vietnam that France expanded into during colonial campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin, a historical northern region of Vietnam during colonial times."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin is a historical region in northern Vietnam referenced in Baron's focus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin is a historical region of northern Vietnam, referenced in Baron's focus and Seventeenth-Century Vietnam sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Northern region of Vietnam; site of French campaigns and the seat of early conflict with Vietnamese forces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonkin refers to the northern region of Vietnam, discussed in Baron's writings and in the Views of Seventeenth-Century Vietnam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-61f2f053f1c7eb75498d3b31a687c2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A geographic region in Southeast Asia (including present-day Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia) that was under colonial and wartime occupation during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"A major Buddhist temple complex at Đồng Dương built under Indravarman II; a symbol of Cham religious and cultural prominence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Geographic region (Indochina) occupied by Japan during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region under French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region under French colonial rule; the broader geographical theater for the colonial and post-colonial conflicts described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region under colonial rule referenced in the context of resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region where colonial conflicts occurred and which saw decolonization dynamics during this period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region where colonial rule and later conflict took place; encompasses Vietnam, Laos, Cambodia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina region; context for the decolonization wars and Cold War dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina, the French colony comprising present-day Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia during the period described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina, the Southeast Asian region comprising present-day Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia, the theater of French colonial rule and the Indochina wars."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina; geographic region comprising Vietnam, Laos, and Cambodia, referenced in the context of colonial federation and regional politics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina; region under French colonial rule referred to in the context of the Vietnamese revolutionary movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Khu vực thuộc địa của Pháp ở Đông Nam Á, nơi diễn ra các biến cố liên quan đến chiến tranh và độc lập của Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region of Southeast Asia under French colonial rule; its dissolution in 1954–1955 enabled independent movements and the eventual division of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Significant Buddhist temple/monastery site in Champa built during Indravarman II's reign."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Indochina region (Vietnam, Laos, Cambodia) under varying control during WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Indochina region that was under colonial rule and later occupied by Japan during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Indochina region under French rule; referenced in the context of the federation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Dương (Indochina) is the broader region where these movements operated and organized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Dương (Indochina) is the federation created by France that includes Vietnam, Cambodia, and Laos under colonial administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Dương (Indochina), the broader colonial region where French and Japanese actions intersected with Vietnamese events."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Dương là vùng địa lý nơi Pháp đã kiểm soát thuộc địa và diễn ra các cuộc chiến tranh Đông Dương."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đồng Dương was a major Cham city with a large Buddhist monastery complex attributed to the Indravarman II era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đồng Dương was the site of a major Buddhist monastery complex constructed under Indravarman II."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bc2794dad524831d7084c6c23b70cd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRUNG KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central Vietnam region referenced in territorial arrangements during decolonization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trung Kỳ refers to central Vietnam within Indochina's historical divisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central protectorate region under French rule in central Vietnam, part of the historical Indochina territorial divisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trung Kỳ refers to the central region of Vietnam; within the text it is associated with An Nam and French influence in central Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central region of Vietnam historically under French influence; included in territorial arrangements after negotiations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trung Kỳ (Central Vietnam) is the central Vietnam region mentioned as part of An Nam's designation within the Indochina Federation context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Vietnam region; linked to An Nam in protectorate arrangements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALGÉRIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Algeria; mentioned as the place of exile for a Nguyễn dynasty figure after capture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Algérie (Algeria) is cited as a French colonial territory, illustrating the broader scope of the French empire referenced in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Algérie (Algeria) is mentioned as the place where the Nguyễn emperor Hàm Nghi was exiled by the French."&lt;SEP&gt;"Algérie (Algeria) was the destination of Hàm Nghi's exile at the hands of French authorities after capture in 1888."&lt;SEP&gt;"Algérie (Algeria) was the destination for Emperor Hàm Nghi's exile by French authorities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
