      <data key="d1">"The Black Flag Army, a guerrilla force that fought French colonial forces in Tonkin."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Black Flag Army, a rebel/auxiliary military force employed by the Nguyễn court to resist French expansion in the north and central regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRANCIS GARNIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Francis Garnier was a French commander—one of the two supreme French leaders killed in an ambush against Vietnamese forces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Francis Garnier was a French general who conducted military campaigns in northern Vietnam (Tonkin) and was killed during the conflict with local forces.&lt;SEP&gt;"Francis Garnier was a French military commander and one of the supreme commanders in the Tonkin period; he was killed in an ambush by forces allied with the Black Flag Army."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HENRI RIVIÈRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Henri Rivière was a French colonial official and military commander in Bắc Kỳ who faced Vietnamese resistance during the late 19th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Henri Rivière was a French commander—one of the two supreme French leaders killed in an ambush against Vietnamese forces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Henri Rivière was a French military commander and the other French supreme commander in Tonkin, who was killed in an ambush during engagement with Vietnamese forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TÂY BAN NHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Province where Renou administered; site of operations and the killing of Renou."&lt;SEP&gt;"Province where Renou served as governor and where conflict occurred during the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spain; allied with France in the 1858–60s campaign against Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spain; colonial power that administered the Philippines and influenced regional dynamics in Southeast Asia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tây Ban Nha (Spain) is referenced as the colonial power associated with the Philippines in the era described, contextualizing regional diplomacy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tây Ban Nha (Spain) participated in the 1862 Saigon Treaty alongside France, affecting territorial arrangements in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tây Ban Nha (Spain) participated in the 1862 Saigon treaty alongside France and the Huế court."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tây Ban Nha is a European country that formed part of the Franco-Spanish expeditionary force against Vietnam during 1858-1862."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tây Ninh was a site of clashes; Renou, the French official, was the governor there during the uprising.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88c2283fe59c1e2798b0a0aafedc3142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VƯƠNG QUỐC CAMPUCHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kingdom of Cambodia, the Cambodian monarchy within the Indochina framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vương quốc Campuchia was restored under French influence and later incorporated into Indochina's federation (Đông Dương)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CẦN VƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broad Vietnamese royalist movement aiming to expel the French and restore traditional social order, linked to the Nghĩa quân."&lt;SEP&gt;"A royalist insurgency movement seeking to restore the Nguyễn monarchy and expel the French."&lt;SEP&gt;"A royalist resistance movement aiming to restore royal authority and expel French rule, linked to Nghĩa quân."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cần Vương was a long-running anti-French movement rooted in royalist and traditionalist circles, contributing to sustained resistance against colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cần Vương was a royalist/anti-colonial movement aimed at expelling French forces and restoring the Nguyễn monarchy.&lt;SEP&gt;"Can Vuong movement, a royalist resistance against French colonial rule, associated with the Can Vuong chiếu and broader anti-colonial campaigns."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3e2d86a8a15344ff5c25829117f928c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THÀNH THÁI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Nguyễn dynasty king who was deposed and exiled for anti-French sentiment; his downfall reflects colonial intervention in the monarchy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor Thành Thái of the Nguyễn dynasty; deposed by the French for anti-colonial attitudes and exiled to Africa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Thành Thái, a Nguyễn dynasty king who was deposed and exiled to Africa for anti-French sentiment, with the pretext of mental illness."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Nguyễn dynasty kings who was deposed and exiled due to anti-French sentiment, illustrating royal backlash against colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thành Thái was a Vietnamese Nguyễn dynasty emperor who was deposed and exiled to Africa for anti-French sentiments, illustrating internal royal dissent against colonial rule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUY TÂN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Nguyễn dynasty king associated with anti-French activities; he was deposed and later captured during a plan to revolt with Trần Cao Vân."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another Nguyễn king who was deposed and exiled for anti-French activities; later involved in conspiracies and political maneuvering."&lt;SEP&gt;"Duy Tân was a Nguyễn dynasty emperor who was deposed and later arrested for involvement in anti-French conspiracies alongside Trần Cao Vân, highlighting the monarchic resistance to French dominance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor Duy Tân noted for reformist ideas; later exiled to Africa for anti-French activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN CAO VÂN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese royalist reformer who conspired with Duy Tân to initiate an uprising against French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese scholar who collaborated with reformist movements; participated in attempted uprisings with Duy Tân and was involved in conspiracies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Royalist figure who collaborated with Duy Tân in anti-French efforts and participated in attempted uprisings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Cao Vân was a patriot and scholar-official who coordinated with Duy Tân in plans for a revolt against French rule, representing intellectual-led resistance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG KINH NGHĨA THỤC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patriotic school in Hanoi founded in 1907 by Phan Châu Trinh, Lương Văn Can, and Nguyễn Quyền to modernize education and promote anti-colonial ideas; it offered free tuition and used Western texts."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patriotic school in Hanoi promoting modern education and reform, with leadership from figures like Lương Văn Can and Phan Châu Trinh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Kinh Nghĩa Thục was a patriotic reform school founded in Hanoi in 1907 by Phan Châu Trinh with Lương Văn Can and Nguyễn Quyền to promote modern civic education and weaken feudal norms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patriotic school in Hanoi promoting modernization, civic education, and reform; hosted terms and instruction encouraging Western knowledge while renouncing old Confucianism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHAN BỘI CHÂU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A leading Vietnamese nationalist and reformist who founded or helped found multiple organizations (Đông Du, Duy Tân hội, Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội) and advocated modernization and independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"A leading Vietnamese nationalist and reformist who organized Đông Du and co-founded Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"A leading Vietnamese nationalist and revolutionary who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou to advocate armed struggle against French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leading Vietnamese nationalist who organized revolutionary activities in Japan and helped shape modern Vietnamese nationalism (co-founded groups like Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu was a Vietnamese nationalist leader who launched the Đông Du movement and helped establish revolutionary organizations in Japan, including Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu was a Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded the Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou and organized armed resistance against French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu is a Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou to pursue modernization and armed efforts to end French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu was a Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou to oppose French colonial rule; he planned armed struggle, was kidnapped by French agents in Shanghai in 1925, and later placed under house arrest at Bến Ngự in Huế until his death in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist revolutionary who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou; kidnapped in Shanghai in 1925 and later imprisoned in Huế."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Bội Châu is a historical Vietnamese reformist and nationalist figure, invoked in the passage as a potential symbol of national salvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese revolutionary leader who founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội in Guangzhou and led anti-French nationalist activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KỲ NGOẠI HẦU CƯỜNG ĐỂ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Nguyễn dynasty noble who co-founded revolutionary organizations in Japan (Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kỳ Ngoại hầu Cường Để was a nationalist figure who collaborated with Phan Bội Châu in founding revolutionary groups such as Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese noble who collaborated with Phan Bội Châu to establish revolutionary organizations in Japan, including Duy Tân Hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese mandarins who collaborated with Phan Bội Châu in founding revolutionary organizations in Japan (Duy Tân hội and Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
