      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A revolutionary organization founded in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and Cuong Để as part of the Duy Tan reform movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A revolutionary organization founded in Japan to promote independence and reforms in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Duy Tân hội is a revolutionary organization in Japan co-founded by Phan Bội Châu and associates to promote reform and national independence in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"A revolutionary organization founded in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and allies to promote modernization and anti-colonial goals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIỆT NAM CÔNG HIẾN HỘI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A revolutionary organization founded in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and Cuong Để."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another revolutionary organization founded in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and Kỳ Ngoại hầu Cường Để advocating constitutional reforms and independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam Công Hiến Hội is a revolutionary organization established in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and partners to advance Vietnamese independence and modernization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another revolutionary organization founded in Japan by Phan Bội Châu and allies; part of the network supporting independence efforts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG DU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A movement/network that sent Vietnamese youth to Japan for modernization and nationalist training; linked to Phan Bội Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Du was a reform movement initiated by Phan Bội Châu in 1905 to modernize Vietnam by sending Vietnamese youth to Japan to study Western knowledge and systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"An early-20th-century reformist movement led by Phan Bội Châu that organized sending Vietnamese youths to Japan to study modern knowledge."&lt;SEP&gt;"A reform movement initiated by Phan Bội Châu to educate Vietnamese youth in Japan and prepare leadership for future independence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bcac0a2ed12c8c14d19b01dcb829b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LƯƠNG VĂN CAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scholar and educator who served as Hiệu trưởng (principal) of Đông Kinh Nghĩa Thục and contributed to its leadership and curriculum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scholar who served as the principal (Hiệu trưởng) of Đông Kinh Nghĩa Thục."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lương Văn Can served as the Hiệu trưởng (principal) of Đông Kinh Nghĩa Thục, playing a leading role in directing its reformist educational mission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patriotic educator who served as the headmaster of Đông Kinh Nghĩa Thục and led its reform efforts."</data>
