    <node id="&quot;TỰ LỰC VĂN ĐOÀN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese literary group prominent in early 20th century literature, promoting modern prose and producing numerous novels as part of Vietnam’s literary awakening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Literary group central to modern Vietnamese literature and nationalist cultural awakening."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pioneering Vietnamese literary group in the early 20th century that helped drive the modernization of prose and intellectual reform."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tự Lực Văn đoàn was a Vietnamese literary group that promoted modern Vietnamese literature and social reform in the early 20th century."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIỆT NAM QUANG PHỤC HỘI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese nationalist organization founded by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou to oppose French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nationalist anti-colonial society founded by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou, aimed at restoring Vietnam’s independence through reform and revolutionary action."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nationalist revolutionary society founded by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou to lead armed resistance against French colonial rule in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam Quang phục Hội was founded by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou as a reformist revolutionary group pushing modernization and resistance to French rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Nam Quang phục Hội was a nationalist organization founded by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou to oppose French colonial rule and mobilize popular support for independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist society established by Phan Bội Châu in Guangzhou to advocate independence from French colonial rule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUẢNG CHÂU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historical region linked with the administrative and military reorganizations in the area by various Chinese powers, including Đông Ngô and later imperial authorities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chinese-administered region; its status and governance were altered under Đông Ngô."&lt;SEP&gt;"City in southern China where Phan Bội Châu established the Việt Nam Quang phục Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"Căn cứ quân sự phía tây bắc biên giới, nơi diễn ra trận đánh và cuộc xâm lược của Tống."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guangzhou, China, where Phan Bội Châu organized early anti-colonial activity and established the Việt Nam Quang phục Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guangzhou, China; birthplace of the anti-French Vietnamese nationalist organizing activity by Phan Bội Châu."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guangzhou, a city in southern China where Vietnamese nationalist groups operated in the early 20th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quảng Châu (Guangzhou) is the Chinese city where Phan Bội Châu founded Việt Nam Quang phục Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quảng Châu (Guangzhou) was the city where Phan Bội Châu founded the Việt Nam Quang phục Hội."&lt;SEP&gt;"Region that was separated into a separate prefecture during the period of Đông Ngô rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ung Châu was one of the border bases raided by Đại Việt forces in 1075 as part of the campaign against the Song dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ung Châu was one of the three Song border bases attacked by Đại Việt during the 1075–1076 campaign."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ung Châu, important Song base attacked by Đại Việt in 1075."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01995274690fe1835d7836e3a481a678&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-277e0e3e66eb14031c1d448dfa63e42c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THƯỢNG HẢI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shanghai, China, where Phan Bội Châu was kidnapped by French agents in 1925 and forcibly returned to Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shanghai; Chinese city where Phan Bội Châu was kidnapped by French agents in 1925 and transported to Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shanghai, China; the city where Phan Bội Châu was kidnapped by French agents in 1925 and transported back to Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shanghai, where Phan Bội Châu was kidnapped by French agents in 1925."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shanghai, a major city where Vietnamese activists operated and where Phan Bội Châu was kidnapped in 1925."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BẾN NGỰ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bến Ngự in Huế was the place where Phan Bội Châu was detained (giam lỏng) by colonial authorities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bến Ngự in Huế, Vietnam, where Phan Bội Châu was placed under house arrest until his death in 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bến Ngự, a detention site in Huế where Phan Bội Châu was imprisoned."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bến Ngự, a historic location in Huế, referenced in exile and administrative contexts during the anti-colonial period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bến Ngự, in Huế, where Phan Bội Châu was kept under house arrest until his death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUỐC DÂN ĐẢNG TRUNG QUỐC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"China's Kuomintang; VNQDĐ was modeled after this party's organizational approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"China's Kuomintang; VNQDĐ was modeled after this party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kuomintang of China, the model used by VNQDĐ for its organization and tactics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kuomintang of China; served as the model/inspiration for VNQDĐ's organization and tactics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chinese Kuomintang, used as a model for VNQDĐ's organizational structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KHỞI NGHĨA YÊN BÁI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1930 armed uprising by VNQDĐ in Bắc Kỳ; failed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yên Bái Uprising of 1930, a VNQDĐ-led armed revolt in Bắc Kỳ that failed and led to harsh repression."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Yen Bai uprising of 1930, organized by VNQDĐ, was crushed by French authorities; its failure led to arrests of leaders."&lt;SEP&gt;"A 1930 uprising by VNQDĐ against French colonial rule in northern Vietnam; ultimately suppressed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN THÁI HỌC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chairman (leader) of VNQDĐ; key organizer of Yen Bai uprising; captured and executed by the French."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leader (Chủ tịch) of VNQDĐ who was captured and executed by colonial authorities following the Yen Bai uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chairman of Việt Nam Quốc Dân Đảng (VNQDĐ) and a key leader who was captured and executed by the French after the Yen Bai uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chairman of Việt Nam Quốc Dân Đảng (VNQDĐ); key leader behind the Yen Bai uprising against the French colonial rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Thái Học, chairman of VNQDĐ; a leading figure who was captured and executed after the Yen Bai uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leader and chairman of VNQDĐ who orchestrated the Yên Bái uprising; executed by French colonial authorities after its failure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẢNG CỘNG SẢN VIỆT NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Communist Party of Vietnam; ideological and political leadership body during and after reunification."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, formed through the unification of several Vietnamese communist groups under Comintern influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam; ruling party guiding reunification and postwar policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam's Communist Party, leading the North Vietnamese government and war effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, the ruling party guiding Vietnam's political system and leadership appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese Communist Party formed through unification of several Vietnamese communist groups under Comintern influence; later renamed during the period of consolidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Communist Party of Vietnam; ruling party of Vietnam; holds central leadership and guides the political system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, referenced as the successor political force and historical context of the movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The party formed through Comintern-guided unification of Đông Dương Cộng sản Đảng, An Nam Cộng sản Đảng, and Đông Dương Cộng sản Liên đoàn; later renamed under Comintern policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, the ruling party whose leadership shapes the country's political system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam; the ruling party responsible for major policy shifts such as Đổi Mới."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese Communist Party formed in the early 20th century; it was later renamed following Comintern guidance under Stalin to Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam is the Vietnamese Communist Party that emerged in the broader historical context referenced in the text (formation context dated to 1930)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam là đảng cầm quyền, lãnh đạo chính sách và định hướng quá trình tái thiết và thống nhất đất nước."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, formed through the unification of several Vietnamese communist groups under Comintern's guidance in the early 1930s."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, the leading political force behind the revolution and governance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam, the ruling party, guiding the state and government leadership, including the General Secretary and central leadership."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam; its leadership guided postwar consolidation and Vietnam's political realignment.&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of Vietnam; successor to Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương and central to the Việt Minh alliance and independence movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam (Communist Party of Vietnam) is cited as the leadership behind the movement since its founding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e1e11930ab01fb061749acffe85b755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4549a0a33a97f39084dfcd2d857e18f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3c75fb34fd08ca28a6bdea4defc0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4820a393047d71ddfc9dd25445f040a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe0d1be514abeb684ef939716ecf874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẢNG CỘNG SẢN ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A name used for the Indochina Communist Party before the unification; later merged into the Vietnamese Communist Party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Communist Party of Indochina; predecessor to the Vietnamese Communist Party, active in anti-colonial and independence movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Communist Party, an early Vietnamese communist organization that later contributed to the formation of the CPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochinese Communist Party, the overarching communist party operating in French Indochina, under whose authority the Nam Kỳ Xứ ủy functions and which supported the anti-French and anti-Japanese struggle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochinese Communist Party, the revolutionary organization that led anti-colonial activities and inspired actions like the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochinese Communist Party that led the Nam Kỳ uprising and related revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochinese Communist Party, the key revolutionary organization leading anti-colonial actions and shaping the independence movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochinese Communist Party, the renamed form of the Vietnamese Communist Party after Comintern influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương is the Indochinese Communist Party, the central authority that oversees and directs the Nam Kỳ regional committee (Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ) and its revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Indochina Communist Party governing body overseeing revolutionary work across French Indochina and coordinating with regional committees such as Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Indochinese Communist Party was a Vietnamese communist organization active under colonial rule. It included party members and allowed political organizations to operate publicly, laying groundwork for nationalist and communist collaboration that would feed into the Việt Minh movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Indochinese Communist Party, the political organization that led the Vietnamese communist movement in French Indochina; it included cadres such as Nguyễn Văn Cừ, Hà Huy Tập, Phan Đăng Lưu, Võ Văn Tần, and Nguyễn Thị Minh Khai."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương (Indochina Communist Party) directed revolutionary activities in the region through its local Trung Kỳ committee."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3c75fb34fd08ca28a6bdea4defc0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐÔNG DƯƠNG CỘNG SẢN ĐẢNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A federation/union of Indochinese communists, part of the early movement leading to CPV formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Communist League; merged into Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam during consolidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Communist Party; one of the early Vietnamese communist groups that later merged into Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Vietnamese communist factions that merged into the Communist Party of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Vietnamese communist groups that merged into the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam as part of the unification process."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Vietnamese communist groups that merged into the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the three early Vietnamese communist groups that emerged in the late 1920s as part of the nationalist–communist movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the three separate Vietnamese communist parties formed in the late 1920s in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông Dương Cộng sản Đảng is an early revolutionary organization that originated in Làng Vân Hải, Nghi Xuân, Hà Tĩnh, alongside Tân Việt Cách mạng Đảng."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đông dương Cộng sản Đảng là một tổ chức cách mạng được nêu trong văn bản."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe0d1be514abeb684ef939716ecf874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AN NAM CỘNG SẢN ĐẢNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An Nam Communist Party; merged into Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam during consolidation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another early Vietnamese communist party forming part of the broader Indochinese communist movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Vietnamese communist groups that merged into the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the three separate Vietnamese communist parties formed in the late 1920s in Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"One of the Vietnamese communist factions that merged into the Communist Party of Vietnam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TẠ THU THÂU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Trotskyist leader in Vietnam who headed the Trotskyist movement in the late 1920s."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leader of the Trotskyist movement in Vietnam; led the Tro-kít faction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tạ Thu Thâu was the Trotskyist leader who headed the Trotskyist movement in Vietnam, contributing to a faction within the early Vietnamese communist movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ta Thu Thau, a leftist figure who led Trotskyist currents (phong trào Trotskít) in Vietnam in the late 1920s."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUỐC TẾ CỘNG SẢN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comintern, the Soviet-led international Communist organization that coordinated with Vietnamese communists and facilitated unification into a single party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soviet-led international communist organization; oversaw the unification of Vietnamese communist groups and directed strategy, including the sending of Nguyễn Ái Quốc to Hong Kong."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist International (Comintern) played a decisive role in guiding, financing and coordinating the Vietnamese communist movement, including unifying several groups into the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam and influencing its later rename."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist International (Comintern), the global communist organization coordinating Communist movements, which directed Vietnamese groups at times."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist International, a Soviet-led international organization that coordinated communist movements and directed the unification of Vietnamese communists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN ÁI QUỐC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alias of Hồ Chí Minh; Vietnamese revolutionary who led the formation of Việt Minh and engaged with Comintern; also linked to founding the French Communist Party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ho Chi Minh; Vietnamese revolutionary who led the unification of Vietnamese communist groups and was sent by Comintern to Hong Kong to chair a unification conference; (also known as Hồ Chí Minh)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc is an alias of Hồ Chí Minh, referenced to indicate that the public did not initially realize Hồ Chí Minh and Nguyễn Ái Quốc were the same person."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc is the historical name of Hồ Chí Minh; he is identified as the head of the Việt Minh, whose leadership is pivotal in determining the country’s fate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc, also known as Hồ Chí Minh, was a Vietnamese revolutionary who helped found the French Communist Party and later worked for the Communist International; he played a central role in organizing Vietnamese communists and in unifying groups across the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Ái Quốc, who would come to be known as Hồ Chí Minh, was a Vietnamese revolutionary who led the unification conference that formed the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam and participated in multiple national movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese revolutionary who led nationalist and communist movements, later known as Hồ Chí Minh; sent by Comintern to Hong Kong to preside over unification talks and founded the Việt Minh."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HỒNG KÔNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hong Kong served as the venue where the Comintern hosted a conference to unify Vietnamese communist groups into the Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong, where Nguyễn Ái Quốc traveled to convene and coordinate with international communist networks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong; site where Nguyễn Ái Quốc was sent to chair the unification conference for Vietnamese communist groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hong Kong, site used for unification talks under Comintern guidance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẢNG CỘNG SẢN PHÁP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Communist Party of France; part of the broader international communist network affecting Vietnamese revolutionary movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"French Communist Party, co-founded with Nguyễn Ái Quốc as part of his early involvement in European communist movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of France, which Nguyễn Ái Quốc helped found/participate in during his time in France, influencing his later revolutionary work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Communist Party of France, with which Nguyễn Ái Quốc was involved during his time in France in the early career, including co-founding it.&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Communist Party, co-founded by Nguyễn Ái Quốc before his international Communist work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Communist Party; Nguyễn Ái Quốc participated in founding it, illustrating his early involvement with international communism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOÀNG ĐẾ BẢO ĐẠI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bao Dai, the emperor who proclaimed the short-lived Empire of Vietnam and exercised governance during the colonial period and wartime arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor of Vietnam who, under Japanese occupation, announced the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam and appointed Trần Trọng Kim as Prime Minister; abdicated on 25 August 1945 ending the Nguyễn dynasty."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoàng đế Bảo Đại was the emperor who headed the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam during Japanese occupation and who later abdicated following the August 1945 events."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese emperor who proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam during the Japanese-controlled period and appointed leadership during that era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who, under Japanese protection, proclaimed the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam and appointed Trần Trọng Kim as Prime Minister."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Emperor who proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam during the Japanese occupation and appointed leaders to govern the state."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who proclaimed the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam under Japanese occupation and abdicated in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor Bảo Đại, the Vietnamese monarch who abdicated in August 1945 and became a civilian under the name Vĩnh Thụy; his abdication clears the way for Việt Minh to take control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who proclaimed the Đế quốc Việt Nam.&lt;SEP&gt;"Hoàng đế cuối cùng của Nhà Nguyễn; tạm thời tuyên bố Đế quốc Việt Nam dưới sự bảo hộ của quân đội Nhật (1945) và bị buộc thoái vị vào ngày 25 tháng 8 năm 1945, chấm dứt triều đại Nhà Nguyễn."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MẶT TRẬN VIỆT MINH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broad resistance front led by the Vietnamese Communist Party to seek national independence, formed under Hồ Chí Minh's leadership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unified front formed in 1941 by Ho Chi Minh to mobilize nationalist and communist groups; cooperated with OSS for intelligence sharing against Japan."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese broad front organized in 1941, led by the Communist Party, to unite nationalist and communist efforts for independence; later cooperated with OSS for intelligence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist front that led the independence movement and participated in proclaiming independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Việt Minh Front, formed in 1941 as a broad coalition for Vietnamese independence and led in practice by the Communist Party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liên minh các lực lượng Việt Nam hành động cho độc lập; đóng vai trò dẫn đến Tuyên ngôn Độc lập và sự ra đời của VNDCCH."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese independence front established in 1941 by Nguyễn Ái Quốc; cooperated with OSS to share intelligence on Japanese activity during WWII."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OSS (Office of Strategic Services), an Allied intelligence agency mentioned in relation to Việt Minh activities during the wartime period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Office of Strategic Services, a U.S. WWII intelligence agency that cooperated with Việt Minh against Japanese forces in Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Office of Strategic Services, the U.S. wartime intelligence agency that cooperated with Việt Minh to share intelligence on Japanese activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Office of Strategic Services; Việt Minh cooperated with OSS to share intelligence about Japanese activities during World War II."&lt;SEP&gt;"Office of Strategic Services, the US wartime intelligence agency; collaborated with Việt Minh to share information about Japanese operations in Indochina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHÁP VICHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The French Vichy government administering parts of Indochina during WWII."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French colonial administration in Indochina under the Vichy regime, seeking to reassert control after Japanese occupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vichy regime in France, which administered the colonial governance in Indochina under occupying power arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vichy regime of France that administered parts of Indochina before the 1945 coup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vichy France; the collaborationist regime that governed metropolitan France and its colonies during WWII, including Indochina, shaping colonial administration and affecting Vietnamese anti-colonial activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vichy regime—the French government installed in Vichy-ruled territory during WWII, acting as the colonial administration in Indochina under Axis influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vichy regime in France, the colonial administration during World War II that affected Indochina."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Vichy regime, a collaborationist government that controlled parts of French Indochina during WWII."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STALIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joseph Stalin, Soviet leader whose pressure contributed to the Việt Minh publicly identifying as a communist organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joseph Stalin, Soviet leader; his era saw Comintern policies that did not favor nationalist separatism in Indochina, impacting local Communist movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joseph Stalin, the Soviet leader who guided the Communist International (Comintern), influencing global communist strategy and the unification of Vietnamese communist groups under Comintern policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joseph Stalin; Soviet leader who exerted pressure affecting Việt Minh's public communist identity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soviet leader referenced as the figure under whose era the Comintern did not support nationalist strands in some contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soviet leader who pressured the Việt Minh to publicly declare themselves as a communist organization, influencing Vietnam's alignment in the Cold War."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soviet leader whose era influenced Comintern policy and the stance toward nationalist movements in colonial contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stalin, the Soviet leader who pressured the Việt Minh to publicly declare themselves as a communist organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN PHÚ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First General Secretary of the Vietnamese Communist Party after its unification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Phú was the first General Secretary of the Việt Nam Cộng sản Đảng (Communist Party of Vietnam) following unification under Comintern."&lt;SEP&gt;"The first General Secretary of the Indochinese Communist Party, a key early leader in Vietnamese communist organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b60881720494b2801d1866f2d58b8eb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN TRỌNG KIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scholar appointed by Bao Đại as Prime Minister of the government that briefly carried the name Đế quốc Việt Nam in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Trọng Kim was a Vietnamese historian and author of Việt Nam sử lược (Vietnam History: A Brief History)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Trọng Kim was a scholar appointed by Bao Dai to serve as Prime Minister of the short-lived Đế quốc Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"A scholar appointed by Bao Đại to serve as Prime Minister of the Đế quốc Việt Nam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scholar appointed as Prime Minister under the Đế quốc Việt Nam regime."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former prime minister under the Trần Trọng Kim government; organized public rallies such as the one in Hue to bolster Việt Minh support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Học giả được bổ nhiệm làm Thủ tướng Chính phủ Đế quốc Việt Nam trong giai đoạn 1945, dưới sự bảo hộ của Nhật Bản."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Trọng Kim is a Vietnamese politician who led the government of the Empire of Vietnam in 1945; his administration is challenged by Việt Minh and ultimately unable to persist, leading to abdication under pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Trọng Kim is the author of Việt Nam sử lược (1971) referenced in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Trọng Kim, Premier who refused Japanese requests to help maintain order during the transitional period and saw the imperial Vietnamese government as lacking real power."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIỆT MINH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese communist organization referenced as part of the broader struggle against French rule and related to the movement behind the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese communist-led resistance movement that fought the French and led the Viet Minh during the early Indochina War."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese political organization formed to resist French colonial rule and to coordinate various anti-colonial movements leading into the independence era."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese independence movement and Communist-led front that fought French colonial rule and laid groundwork for the DRV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist and communist-led front that mobilized resistance for independence and was the political base of the postwar Vietnamese state."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist and communist-led resistance movement that fought against French colonial rule and led the independence effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist-communist independence movement, active during the First Indochina War and a core political actor in the North; later recognized by the sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist/communist front that led the independence push and represented the Viet Minh government."&lt;SEP&gt;"Independence movement founded to resist French rule; later the political base of VNDCCH; supported by China and USSR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist and communist-led resistance front opposing French colonial rule and later the Transitional Government."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese nationalist-communist alliance that emerged from the Indochinese Communist movement and led the August Revolution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam's nationalist-communist independence movement that led the struggle against French rule and laid groundwork for North Vietnam's governance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese nationalist coalition leading the independence movement and precursor to the Democratic Republic of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Political-military organization leading the Vietnamese independence movement; central to the event and to the provisional government."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese nationalist/communist movement that led resistance against French rule and resisted surrender terms in 1947."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Việt Minh, a Vietnamese nationalist and political alliance formed to seek independence from French colonial rule and to resist occupation; a broad front associated with the Vietnamese independence effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"The broader Vietnamese independence movement associated with the Viet Nam Tuyên truyền Giải phóng quân, which conducted operations against French forces in this episode."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese independence movement and political organization; received support from China and the USSR; public stance shifts under external pressure toward communism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh is a Vietnamese nationalist political organization formed to lead resistance against colonial rule and later Japan; it played a central role in the August Revolution of 1945 and in establishing Vietnam's independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh is a Vietnamese nationalist-communist organization leading the struggle against colonial rule and occupation, and is the central actor in the power transfer described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh is a Vietnamese nationalist-communist resistance organization that led anti-Japanese activities and played a central role in the August Revolution, mobilizing mass support for independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh is the Vietnamese independence front created to unite nationalist and communist forces to oppose Japanese occupation and later French rule. It led mobilizations in August 1945 across northern Vietnam and played a central role in planning the general uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh is the nationalist-revolutionary organization leading the independence movement; it represented the party and its members in the abdication event and the push for an independent Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Việt Minh, the Vietnamese nationalist front leading the struggle against foreign occupation, mobilizing broad popular support and orchestrating the August Revolution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7418e6f1b899c505272caee02f3cf1ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d8e97a0e4680cead04b467abbaf21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f</data>
    </node>
