    <node id="&quot;QUỐC HỘI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Assembly of Vietnam; the legislative body that decided major decisions, including renaming Saigon and unification."&lt;SEP&gt;"National Assembly; the legislative body of Vietnam that decided to rename Saigon to Ho Chi Minh City in 1976."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc hội Pháp là cơ quan lập pháp của Pháp, có vai trò phê duyệt các hiệp ước và các văn kiện liên quan đến Đông Dương."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quốc hội Việt Nam, cơ quan lập pháp, ban hành các chính sách và quyết định quan trọng như sáp nhập miền Nam và đổi tên thành phố."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French National Assembly, which formally ratified treaties such as the Patenôtre agreement and other accords surrounding Vietnam's status."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Assembly of Vietnam, which voted on the first constitution and related matters in 1946."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Assembly of Vietnam; in 1976 it decided to rename the city of Saigon to Ho Chi Minh City as part of postwar reforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Assembly that ratified the first constitution in November 1946 and acted as a key legislative body in the early Vietnamese state."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Assembly that voted to adopt the 1946 constitution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese National Assembly that enacted the 1946 constitution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The legislative body that passed the first constitution of Việt Nam Dân chủ Cộng hòa in 1946."&lt;SEP&gt;"The legislative body that voted to approve the first constitution of Việt Nam Dân chủ Cộng hòa and shaped early state governance."</data>
