    <node id="&quot;NAM KINH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A district in Nghệ An where revolutionary activity took place as part of the movement's base area."&lt;SEP&gt;"A region in northern Vietnam referenced as part of the historical context of the dynastic transition in this narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Đàn in Nghệ An Province is referenced as part of the geographic background related to Nguyễn Ái Quốc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Đàn is a Nghệ An district where Soviet-style local administrations formed as part of the movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Định is a northern Vietnamese province where Trần influence rose during the late Lý period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Định is a northern Vietnamese region mentioned in the historical narrative as part of the geopolitical landscape during the Lý and Trần eras."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Định là vùng khu vực và tỉnh ở miền Bắc Việt Nam, được nhắc tới như nơi các dòng họ và phe phái tập trung quyền lực trong thời Lý–Trần."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Định region is described as a geographic area where political power consolidated in the late Lý period and later during the Trần ascendancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nanjing, China, site of a political alliance formed by anti-communist Vietnamese factions in 1947 to cooperate with France.&lt;SEP&gt;"Nanjing, China; site of a political alliance formation of anti-communist Vietnamese factions in 1947."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nanjing, China; site where Vietnamese anti-communist factions formed a political alliance in 1947, seeking cooperation with France via Bao Dai."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nanjing, China; venue of a political bloc and talks in 1947 involving anti-communist Vietnamese factions allied with France."</data>
