    <node id="&quot;BẢO ĐẠI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bảo Đại was the last emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty who abdicated in August 1945, signaling a shift toward establishing a new governmental order and hoping for a peaceful transition that would unite the nation and be tolerant of opposing parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bảo Đại was the last emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty, who abdicated in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bảo Đại, former Vietnamese monarch who was deposed by Ngô Đình Diệm, leading to VNCH."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bảo Đại, the former emperor of Vietnam, associated with the transitional government alongside Trần Trọng Kim in the post-Sin/World War II period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor and head of state of the State of Vietnam; deposed by Ngô Đình Diệm in 1955 during the transition to Việt Nam Cộng hòa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emperor who abdicated; his abdication is described as part of the ceremony; abdication reported in Hue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former Vietnamese emperor who returns to politics and leads anti-Communist factions allied with France as part of the Nam Kinh alignment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former Vietnamese emperor; reinstated by the French to participate in politics and to symbolize cooperation with France."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former emperor of Vietnam; led anti-communist negotiations and headed the compromise strategy with France (Giải pháp Bảo Đại)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former emperor who played a political role in steering anti-communist factions and served as Quốc trưởng (head of state) for the Vietnamese state during this period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Last emperor of Vietnam; head of state of Quốc gia Việt Nam; deposed in 1955 by Ngô Đình Diệm and his authority subsequently diminished as Việt Nam Cộng hòa took power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Last emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty; abdicated in 1945.&lt;SEP&gt;"Last emperor of the Nguyễn dynasty; head of the State of Vietnam; ousted in 1955 and replaced by Ngô Đình Diệm as head of the Republic of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The last Emperor of Vietnam and head of State of the State of Vietnam until 1955, deposed by Ngô Đình Diệm during the transition to the Republic of Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The last emperor of the Vietnamese monarchy, whose abdication symbolized the end of the monarchy and a shift toward republican rule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebc4b0a454e2ea3adc019759de704c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3692b44304ff5da1927dfcb9ab90461</data>
    </node>
