      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Military Assistance Advisory Group, a US-led force; reorganized in Indochina into country-specific units, including for Vietnam (1955)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BALAZS SZALONTAI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Balazs Szalontai is a historian who used declassified Hungarian diplomatic documents to estimate casualties in North Vietnam during the land reform campaigns (1953–1956)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian who notes the number of landowners executed and imprisoned in the north during land reform campaigns, based on declassified Hungarian diplomatic documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian cited in the text noting land reform executions and punishments in the North during 1953–1956."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian who documented land reform executions in the North (1953–1956) using declassified diplomatic materials from Hungary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDWIN E. MOÏSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edwin E. Moïse is a scholar who estimated casualties in the Vietnam War, with an approximate total around 13,500 deaths including suicides after arrests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edwin E. Moïse is a scholar who estimated the total deaths in the campaigns to be around 13,500, including suicides after arrests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian who estimates total casualties in the land reform campaigns in North Vietnam; referenced in the text as providing casualty estimates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian who estimates total casualties in the land reform campaigns in the North during 1953–1956."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scholar Edwin E. Moïse, who estimated the death toll of the Vietnam War (about 13,500 deaths, including suicides after arrests)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edwin E. Moïse is a scholar who estimated the total number of deaths in the Vietnam conflict, approximately 13,500, including suicides after arrests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scholar who provides casualty estimates for the North's 1953–1956 land reform campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Historian who estimated casualties from North Vietnam's land reform campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edwin E. Moïse was a scholar who estimated the total number of deaths in the Vietnam War at about 13,500, including suicides after arrests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scholar who estimated total fatalities in the North's land reform campaigns."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4549a0a33a97f39084dfcd2d857e18f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUNGARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Country in Central Europe; referenced as the source of declassified diplomatic documents used by researchers in the North Vietnam period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country in Europe; mentioned as the home country of diplomats whose declassified documents were used by a scholar to estimate casualties in North Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hungary is referenced as the source of declassified diplomatic documents used by Balazs Szalontai."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hungary, whose diplomats are referenced in declassified documents cited by historians about North Vietnam's land reform."&lt;SEP&gt;"Country whose diplomats supplied declassified materials referenced by Szalontai."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c715893072e90e3f1536ec249629f939</data>
    </node>
