      <data key="d2">chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53</data>
      <data key="d1">"An Nam đô hộ phủ đổi tên thành Trấn Nam đô hộ phủ (767).", "&lt;SEP&gt;"Renamed form of An Nam đô hộ phủ during a period of administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Name used briefly for the northern protectorate during upheavals; related to An Nam đô hộ phủ.</data>
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAM CHIẾU&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc782d7f1eac567ce6188dd679cd4c53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6033ac15f370150074084b2248ba04f3</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rival force mentioned as being repelled in the early narrative of expansion and defense in Vietnamese history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom in present-day Yunnan that intervened in An Nam and besieged Tống Bình; later defeated by Cao Biền's forces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Chiếu can thiệp vào khu vực Vân Nam, phản ánh sự can thiệp và liên minh tranh giành ảnh hưởng."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Chiếu is a neighboring military power mentioned in the text as being repelled; its actions are part of the early regional conflicts surrounding Đại La Thành."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Chiếu was a historical southern Chiếu state/polity opposing Đại Việt; encountered in the narrative as the invading force resisted by Vietnamese rulers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kingdom in what is today Yunnan; intervened in An Nam and allied with local uprisings.&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Chiếu is a historical army of a southern Chiếu group that invaded Đại Việt and was repelled."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Chiếu was a kingdom in the Yunnan region that intervened in An Nam, inciting local uprisings and influencing northern Vietnam politics."</data>
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
    </node>
