      <data key="d1">"Edited volume (2006) compiling Borri's and Baron's accounts; editors include Dutton, Dror, and Taylor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-61f2f053f1c7eb75498d3b31a687c2e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAM KỲ KHỞI NGHĨA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A large-scale anti-French uprising in southern Vietnam that ultimately failed due to discovery and brutal crackdown, but left a legacy for later Vietnamese independence movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"A large-scale uprising across southern Vietnam against French colonial rule that began on the night of 22 November 1940 and spread to multiple provinces."&lt;SEP&gt;"A major anti-French uprising in southern Vietnam associated with the Indochinese communist movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bắc Sơn uprising served as an inspiration and precedent for the Nam Kỳ uprising, illustrating regional revolutionary influences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa (Southern Vietnam uprising) occurred in late November 1940, spreading from Biên Hòa to Cà Mau as insurgents seized power in numerous provinces and challenged French colonial authorities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa is a 1940 armed uprising in Cochinchina (Nam Kỳ) led and organized by the Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ of the Indochinese Communist Party to oppose French colonial rule and Japanese occupation, mobilizing local peasantry and workers across southern provinces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa is a 1940 armed uprising in southern Vietnam against French colonial rule and Japanese occupation, led by the Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ of the Indochina Communist Party (Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa is an armed uprising in 1940 by the people of Nam Kỳ against French colonial rule and Japanese imperial expansion; it was conceived and led by the Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ of the Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương and involved mass mobilization, preparation, and clandestine resistance activities across Saigon, Chợ Lớn, and surrounding areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa is the armed uprising in Southern Vietnam in 1940 against French colonial rule and Japanese occupation, conceived and led by the Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ of the Indochinese Communist Party."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa was a large-scale uprising across southern Vietnam in late 1940, involving multiple provinces, mass mobilization, and guerrilla actions.&lt;SEP&gt;"Nam Kỳ uprising, a major southern Vietnamese revolt against French colonial rule; though ultimately crushed, it became a symbol of courage and a catalyst for later movements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Nam Kỳ uprising was a major anti-French insurrection in southern Vietnam, led by Vietnamese communists and local groups as part of the broader struggle for independence; it was eventually crushed by French forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XỨ ỦY NAM KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nam Kỳ regional party committee, the governing body coordinating revolutionary strategy and leadership for the uprising in southern Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The regional party committee in southern Vietnam coordinating revolutionary activities and the Nam Kỳ uprising during 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ is a regional branch of the Indochina Communist Party that planned and led the Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa, coordinating local revolutionary activities in southern Vietnam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ is the Nam Kỳ regional committee of the Đảng Cộng sản Đông Dương, responsible for planning and directing local anti-colonial activities including the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ is the regional committee of the Indochinese Communist Party in Southern Vietnam; it planned, organized, and guided activities against French and Japanese domination and coordinated with the central party leadership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ was the regional party committee guiding revolutionary activities and strategic decisions in Southern Vietnam during the Nam Kỳ uprising (1940)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xứ ủy Trung Kỳ is the Trung Kỳ Provincial Committee, a local base of the Indochina Communist Party that directed activities in the area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd3c75fb34fd08ca28a6bdea4defc0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VÕ VĂN TẦN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Communist leader executed during the crackdown on the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Vietnamese revolutionary who was executed during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"A cadre of the Indochinese Communist Party; among those executed during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa."&lt;SEP&gt;"A notable communist leader who was executed during the crackdown on revolutionary leaders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chính phủ Việt Nam operates under the presidency of Võ Văn Thưởng, who has served as President since 2023."&lt;SEP&gt;"Former Xứ ủy secretary who was replaced by Tạ Uyên during the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leader (bí thư) of Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ who drafted the preparation outlines for the anti-French movement and commanded guerrilla activity in the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"President of Vietnam since 2023 (Chủ tịch nước), a top state leadership role in the Vietnamese political system."&lt;SEP&gt;"President of Vietnam since 2023; a key figure in the current state leadership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Previous Bí thư Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ, later replaced by Tạ Uyên."&lt;SEP&gt;"Võ Văn Thưởng has been the President of Vietnam since 2023."&lt;SEP&gt;"Võ Văn Thưởng is the President of Vietnam since 2023, the head of state and a key political figure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Võ Văn Tần was the Bí thư Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ who was later replaced by Tạ Uyên."&lt;SEP&gt;"Võ Văn Tần was the secretary of Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ and directed preparations for the uprising; he also led guerrilla units and was later arrested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Võ Văn Tần was the secretary of the Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ who drafted preparations and directed early actions for the anti-French/anti-Japanese uprising; he was later arrested in the crackdown on the movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e0ff15a988913e85c0426ea19d7198&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VŨ ĐÌNH HIẾU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-ranking party official in Nam Kỳ; arrested in Saigon in 1940 during crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vũ Đình Hiếu was among the leaders arrested in Saigon during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;"Vũ Đình Hiếu, a fellow leader arrested in Saigon during the crackdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHAN ĐĂNG LƯU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese revolutionary and member of the Communist movement who was executed during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"A key Communist leader executed during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Đăng Lưu was a leading figure in the Nam Kỳ uprising and was among those targeted by French authorities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Đăng Lưu was a member of the movement who was sent to the North to liaise with the Central Committee to report and seek approval for the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"A leading figure in the Indochinese movement who was executed during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Đăng Lưu was a representative of the Central Committee of the Indochinese Communist Party; he was involved in coordinating uprising planning and was sent north to report to the central leadership and seek approval for the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolutionary figure who was among those arrested as the uprising unfolded."&lt;SEP&gt;"A cadre of the Indochinese Communist Party mentioned among those executed during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Representative of the Central Committee of the Indochina Communist Party; tasked with coordinating between Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ and central leadership, and later sent to the North to report and seek approval for the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolutionary leader who was arrested by the French during the uprising."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHAN VĂN VOI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Party leader in Nam Kỳ who was arrested in 1940 during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Văn Voi was among the cadres arrested by the French authorities as part of the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Văn Voi, a participant in the uprising arrested during the crackdown in Saigon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHẠM CHUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Party official arrested in 1940 during the crackdown in Saigon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phạm Chung was among the cadres arrested by the French authorities as part of the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;"Phạm Chung, another listed individual arrested during the crackdown in 1940."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN THỊ MINH KHAI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese revolutionary and female leader in the Indochinese Communist movement who was executed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A female Vietnamese Communist leader executed during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Thị Minh Khai, a Nam Kỳ Xứ ủy member and Saigon-Chợ Lớn party secretary; arrested in Chợ Lớn on July 30, 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"A female communist leader who was executed as part of the crackdown on revolutionaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nguyễn Thị Minh Khai, Ủy viên Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ and Bí thư Thành ủy Sài Gòn - Chợ Lớn, was arrested on 30 July 1940 at Chợ Lớn.&lt;SEP&gt;"A cadre of the Indochinese Communist Party; among those executed during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ khởi nghĩa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Member of Xứ ủy Nam kỳ and Bí thư Thành ủy Sài Gòn - Chợ Lớn (Saigon-Chợ Lớn city party secretary)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TẠ UYÊN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bí thư Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ who replaced Võ Văn Tần as leader of the Xứ ủy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bí thư Xứ ủy who replaced Võ Văn Tần as Xứ ủy secretary during the uprising; later arrested as part of the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tạ Uyên became Bí thư Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ after replacing Võ Văn Tần; involved in leadership during the uprising and subsequent arrests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tạ Uyên, who served as secretary of the Nam Kỳ Xứ ủy during the preparation period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tạ Uyên was elected as Bí thư Xứ ủy Nam Kỳ during the extended meeting, succeeding Võ Văn Tần in leadership."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BA SON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A large Saigon factory site mentioned as a base where guerrilla activities were developed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ba Son is a large industrial site in Sài Gòn where guerrilla activities and arms production took place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ba Son is a prominent shipyard and industrial facility in Saigon that functioned as a site of industrial support and mobilization context for revolutionary activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;F.A.C.I.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Saigon-based industrial facility/factory referenced as a site for guerrilla network development."&lt;SEP&gt;"F.A.C.I. is an industrial facility in Saigon mentioned alongside other production sites contributing to the anti-colonial effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"F.A.C.I. is one of the large enterprises in Sài Gòn mentioned as a site for guerrilla activity and arms production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHỢ QUÁN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chợ Quán is a locality in Saigon mentioned as part of the uprising's logistical network."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chợ Quán is a location in Saigon associated with revolutionary activity and arms logistics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRƯỜNG BÁCH NGHỆ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A school in Saigon that served as part of revolutionary network infrastructure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trường Bách Nghệ is a school in Saigon cited among sites of revolutionary activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trường Bách Nghệ was a notable vocational school in Saigon mentioned among the places connected to the movement's organization and logistics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MÓP XANH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A location in Tân An where bomb-making and arms production occurred for the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Móp Xanh (Tân An) is a location noted for weapon production and clandestine arms-related activities during the period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Móp Xanh (Tân An) is a rural area noted for weapons manufacturing during the uprising."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MỸ THO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A town in southern Vietnam; site of a key planning meeting (Hội nghị mở rộng) related to the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"City in the Mekong Delta; 54 of 56 xã in Mỹ Tho were seized during the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key southern city where the uprising occurred; 54 of 56 communes were seized by the insurgents in Mỹ Tho."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mỹ Tho is a locality associated with the uprising; includes places like Bà U and Móp Xanh."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mỹ Tho was a major site of the uprising where 54 of 56 xã were captured and guerrilla forces fought against the French.&lt;SEP&gt;"Mỹ Tho is a southern Vietnamese city referenced as a site of revolutionary activity and organizational presence during the Nam Kỳ uprising period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHÙA HÒA THƯỢNG ĐỒNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chùa Hòa thượng Đồng is a temple cited in connection with clandestine networks and strikes linked to the uprising area around Rạch Giá."&lt;SEP&gt;"chùa Hòa thượng Đồng is a temple in Rạch Giá mentioned in the uprising narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RẠCH GIÁ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"City in southern Vietnam involved in the revolutionary efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rạch Giá is a coastal location in the Mekong Delta region mentioned in connection with arms production facilities or clandestine operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rạch Giá is a coastal town involved in the uprising context through the temple and other sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HÓC MÔN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"District in Gia Định where guerrilla actions and engagements occurred."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hóc Môn district is referenced as a site near which some arrests and activities occurred during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hóc Môn is a district where Võ Văn Tần was arrested during the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hóc Môn was a focal point of guerrilla actions; rebels attacked and contended with French forces there."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hóc Môn, a district of Saigon where leaders were arrested and where revolutionary activity occurred."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHỢ LỚN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A district in Saigon that housed the Saigon-Chợ Lớn city party leadership and served as a base for revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chợ Lớn is a key urban district in Saigon where major arrests occurred and where Nguyễn Thị Minh Khai and Nguyễn Hữu Tiến were captured; it served as a administrative center for Saigon-Chợ Lớn.&lt;SEP&gt;"Chợ Lớn is the Saigon district where Nguyễn Hữu Tiến and Nguyễn Thị Minh Khai were arrested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chợ Lớn saw significant uprising activity with rebels capturing many tổng (districts) as part of the broader revolt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Major area in Saigon where insurgent forces gained control over many communes."&lt;SEP&gt;"District of Saigon where the uprising captured many administrative units."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HỘI NGHỊ TRUNG ƯƠNG LẦN THỨ VII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hội nghị Trung ương lần thứ VII is a Central Committee meeting where the uprising was discussed; it concluded conditions were not yet ripe and influenced the timing and leadership decisions, including dispatching Phan Đăng Lưu North for reporting and seeking approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Seventh Central Conference of the Indochinese Communist Party, where central directives were discussed and decisions about the uprising were made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seventh Central Committee meeting of the Indochina Communist Party to report and obtain instructions on revolutionary strategy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRUNG ƯƠNG ĐẢNG CỘNG SẢN ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central Committee of the Indochinese Communist Party, the overarching leadership referenced in central decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Central Committee of the Indochinese Communist Party, which supervised the southern regional committee and guided overall strategy against French and Japanese rule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THƯỜNG VỤ XỨ ỦY NAM KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Executive committee of the Nam Kỳ regional party; directed the Xứ ủy's activities and decisions during the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thường vụ Xứ ủy Nam kỳ is the executive body of the Nam Kỳ regional party committee; it issued the order to start the uprising on the night of 22 November 1940 and coordinated plans and actions with local insurgent bodies to seize power from the French colonial authorities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HỘI NGHỊ MỞ RỘNG Ở MỸ THO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded conference in Mỹ Tho to discuss and plan the uprising and coordinate actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Expanded meeting held in Mỹ Tho to discuss the uprising and decide on actions; resulted in Phan Đăng Lưu being sent to the North to liaise with the Central Committee."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐỨC QUỐC XÃ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Đức Quốc Xã (Nazi Germany) is the regime that invaded France in 1940, creating the broader wartime context referenced in the historical overview."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TÂN XUÂN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A village in Hóc Môn where Võ Văn Tần was arrested as part of the crackdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Xuân is a commune in Hóc Môn district; arrest site of Võ Văn Tần."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Xuân is a commune in Hóc Môn district; mentioned as the arrest location of Võ Văn Tần on 21 April 1940."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Xuân is a rural area near Hóc Môn where arrests occurred during the crackdown on the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Xuân was mentioned as part of the area around Hóc Môn involved in arrests during the crackdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NHÀ ĐÈN CHỢ QUÁN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A location in Chợ Quán, Saigon, used as a local base of operation for revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà đèn Chợ Quán is a Saigon location mentioned among revolutionary sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà đèn Chợ Quán is a location in Saigon cited among the uprising's logistical and revolutionary activity sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà đèn Chợ Quán is a notable site in Saigon tied to the uprising activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nhà đèn Chợ Quán is a location in Saigon referenced as part of urban infrastructure and the revolutionary movement's sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-750f8e96d1bcbbd9a06d573268723339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRƯỞNG BAN KHỞI NGHĨA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trưởng ban khởi nghĩa was the head of the Nam Kỳ uprising, coordinating the planning and execution of the rebellion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;160 ĐƯỜNG DAYOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"160 Dayot Street (now Nguyễn Thái Bình) is the meeting place where Nguyễn Như Hạnh heard the lệnh khởi nghĩa and where key leaders discussed the uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"Street in Saigon (now Nguyễn Thái Bình) where Bí thư Thành ủy Nguyễn Như Hạnh met uprising organizers to hear the order."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHAN NHUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Thành ủy member who was captured by Phòng nhì Pháp."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Thành ủy viên who was captured as the crackdown began."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phan Nhung, Thành ủy viên, was arrested (along with about 50 others) by Phòng nhì Pháp during the crackdown surrounding the uprising."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65a62981dbf13b2b72920ca1960170b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHÒNG NHÌ PHÁP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phòng nhì Pháp (French Police) was the colonial security force responsible for arresting Nam Kỳ uprising members."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French police Division II, responsible for surveillance and arrests of revolutionaries during the Nam Kỳ uprising."&lt;SEP&gt;"The French Second Bureau, the colonial counterintelligence service responsible for tracking and capturing insurgents."</data>
