    <node id="&quot;VIỆT NAM TUYÊN TRUYỀN GIẢI PHÓNG QUÂN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Vietnamese liberation army and propaganda arm connected to the independence movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Việt Nam Tuyên truyền Giải phóng quân is the Vietnamese revolutionary organization (Viet Minh) that organized and carried out attacks on French outposts Phai Khắt and Nà Ngần during the December 1944 battles; it later became part of the broader Vietnamese resistance movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnam's propaganda-liberation army, a revolutionary military organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"An organization associated with the broader independence movement and revolutionary activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnamese revolutionary organization that conducted guerrilla attacks against French fortresses during 1944, including the attacks on Phai Khắt and Nà Ngần; its actions were aimed at disrupting French colonial control in Cao Bằng province."&lt;SEP&gt;"In December 1944, the Viet Nam Tuyên truyền Giải phóng quân (the Viet Minh armed force) conducted two early battles against French forts Phai Khắt and Nà Ngần, capturing soldiers and a fort commander; these actions were commanded by Võ Nguyên Giáp and marked an early, organized Viet Minh military operation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Vietnam Propaganda and Liberation Army, the military component of the Vietnamese independence movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7418e6f1b899c505272caee02f3cf1ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0d2b12d6dc3ace3b2354166252a164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CÁCH MẠNG THÁNG TÁM 1945&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"August Revolution that prepared the ground for Vietnamese independence and the Việt Minh movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cách mạng tháng Tám (August Revolution), the uprising that led to Vietnam's independence and a shift in power."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution of 1945 that toppled colonial rule and led to the creation of a Vietnamese republic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution of 1945, a key turning point toward Vietnamese independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution of 1945, a pivotal national uprising leading to independence; referenced as a subsequent milestone in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution of 1945, a pivotal step toward Vietnamese independence and the birth of the Vietnamese state."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution, a key historical event referenced in the broader context of Vietnamese history."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution, a major event in Vietnamese history referenced in the broader historical context of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The August Revolution, a pivotal national uprising that led toward independence and drew lessons from the Nam Kỳ uprising."</data>
