    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MÓNG CÁI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A border town in Quảng Ninh province, near the Chinese border; mentioned as part of the Hải Ninh–Móng Cái area during power handovers in the August Revolution period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18d8e97a0e4680cead04b467abbaf21b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TÂN TRÀO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Town in northern Vietnam where the National Congress was held on August 13, 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Trào is a location in northern Vietnam where Việt Minh planned the August Revolution and organized revolutionary activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tân Trào is the rural locality from which Hồ Chí Minh traveled to Hanoi, underscoring the movement of the independence leadership toward the capital."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KHÂM SAI BẮC KỲ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Khâm sai Bắc Kỳ was a colonial administrative post in Bắc Kỳ region; oversaw local governance under Japanese administration, later implicated in interactions with Việt Minh."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SỞ BẢO AN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sở Bảo An was the local security bureau in colonial Indochina, enforcing order and suppressing dissent during WWII."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SỞ MẬT THÁM TRUNG ƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Central Security Bureau responsible for intelligence and counterintelligence operations across Vietnam during the wartime period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SỞ KIỂM DUYỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Censorship Office controlling information and publications in the colonial administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHỦ TOÀN QUYỀN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Governor-General's Palace where Japanese forces set up machine guns and security was deployed around the ceremony."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phủ Toàn quyền (Governor-General's Palace) in Hanoi is the ceremonial and administrative backdrop for the events, with security arrangements and representatives like Jean Sainteny present nearby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phủ Toàn quyền (Governor-General's Palace) in Hanoi is the ceremonial backdrop for events and security arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Governor-General's Office, the top colonial administrative authority in Indochina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGÂN HÀNG ĐÔNG DƯƠNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indochina Bank, a financial institution whose control was contested by Việt Minh and the Japanese, prompting joint protection arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indochina Bank; financial institution under colonial oversight during WWII, involved in currency and economy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ngân hàng Đông Dương (Indochina Bank), an important colonial financial institution mentioned in the context of the era's power structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fff36ca9411ec2bf48b0a366dd7589f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NẠN ĐÓI KHỦNG KHIẾP 1944-1945&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A catastrophic famine during Japanese occupation across parts of Vietnam causing mass starvation and deaths, heightening revolutionary support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Famine in northern and central Vietnam during 1944–1945, causing hundreds of thousands to millions of deaths."&lt;SEP&gt;"Severe famine across northern and central Vietnam causing large casualties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6322ad53528ea4e193eaf9be34d2898</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2 TRIỆU NGƯỜI CHẾT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The famine that killed roughly two million people, accelerating popular support for Việt Minh."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3c3dccc1bdcf6bd8ef4c192da6a818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRƯỜNG CHINH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prominent Vietnamese revolutionary leader who participated in the Tan Trao conference and is described as a key organizer in the uprising planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOÀNG QUỐC VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vietnamese revolutionary and political figure who participated in the Tan Trao conference and contributed to the uprising planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGUYỄN LƯƠNG BẰNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nguyễn Lương Bằng presented Bao Đại with the red flag and star insignia, illustrating involvement of Việt Minh-era figures in the ceremonial honors surrounding the abdication and the independence movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Representative of the Tổng bộ Việt Minh; speaks about unification and fighting for independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vietnamese revolutionary and official who attended the Tan Trao conference and helped shape discussions on the conditions for the uprising."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0858721f576cf19954031c342a7d2bff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
