      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIỆT MINH HOÀNG DIỆU HÀ NỘI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Việt Minh Hoàng Diệu Hà Nội militia provided protection during mobilizations in Hanoi."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BỘ NỘI VỤ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ministry of Interior under the Trần Trọng Kim government."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHÍNH PHỦ TRẦN TRỌNG KIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The government led by Trần Trọng Kim, coordinating public mobilization and Việt Minh alignment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN ĐÌNH NAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trần Đình Nam is a figure who dares to demand the king abdicate, prompting strict condemnation from others in the political debate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Đình Nam was the Minister of Interior in the Trần Trọng Kim government."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERAUCHI HISAICHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terauchi Hisaichi was the Japanese field marshal and commander of the Southern Army who pledged non-intervention if Việt Minh seized power and coordinated with Việt Minh leaders in Saigon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRẦN VĂN GIÀU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trần Văn Giàu was a senior Việt Minh representative in Saigon, a key negotiator with the Japanese in 1945."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trần Văn Giàu, Chairman of the Nam Bộ Administrative Committee (Lâm ủy hành chính Nam Bộ) who urged national unity and vigilance against colonial attempts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHẠM NGỌC THẠCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phạm Ngọc Thạch was a senior Việt Minh official who, alongside Trần Văn Giàu, represented Việt Minh interests in Saigon negotiations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phạm Ngọc Thạch, a physician who was appointed Minister of Health in the Provisional Government and sworn to lead the country and defend independence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f9c5b331f58bfebf51e7a9e8de7972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUỲNH PHÚ SỔ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Huỳnh Phú Sổ was a leader who united several political-religious organizations into a broader front and helped organize large-scale demonstrations in Saigon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NGỌ MÔN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ngọ Môn is the gate at the southern entrance of the Imperial City in Huế, where the abdication ceremony was observed as the king read the abdication declaration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ngọ Môn is the gate of the Imperial City where the abdication announcement is publicly read."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THANH NIÊN TIỀN PHONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thanh niên Tiền phong is a nationalist youth organization that, along with Việt Minh, forms the core of the Saigon protests and power seizure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thanh niên tiền tuyến was a youth organization contributing to the nationwide uprising."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3bfa206adeee22a1ede2ef2ae0ad9711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAO ĐÀI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cao Đài is a major religious-political organization that joined the coalition forming the National Front in the South.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOÀ HẢO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hoà Hảo is another religious organization allied with the coalition forming the National Front in the South.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐẠI VIỆT QUỐC DÂN ĐẢNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Đại Việt Quốc dân đảng is one of the political groups that joined the coalition forming the National Front in the South.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MẶT TRẬN QUỐC GIA VIỆT NAM THỐNG NHẤT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mặt trận Quốc gia Việt Nam Thống nhất is the National United Front formed by uniting several groups and leading protests and power consolidation in the South."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUỘC CÁCH MẠNG THÁNG 8 NĂM 1945&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The August Revolution, a pivotal uprising that led to the formation of Việt Minh-led government and the Democratic Republic of Vietnam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHẠM KHẮC HÒE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A high-ranking court official who invokes a prophecy about Bảo Đại's abdication, illustrating traditional influence in political decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUYÊN NGÔN THOÁI VỊ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The official abdication declaration by Emperor Bảo Đại, signaling a transfer of power to Việt Minh."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ĐỒNG NAI THƯỢNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A southern province that was among the last to come under Việt Minh control during the August 1945 power transfer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HÀ TIÊN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another southern province that Việt Minh captured as part of consolidating control in the South."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bf0b29bf76d345dfa9da0349d9f546d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JEAN SAINTENY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jean Sainteny was a senior official of Free French (France libre) who attended the Hanoi events, observed the crowds, and interacted with the Vietnamese leadership at the Governor-General's Palace."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VĨNH THỤY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vĩnh Thụy is the personal name used for Bao Đại; the text refers to a citizen named Vĩnh Thụy who received the insignia on behalf of the Việt Minh.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUẢNG TRƯỜNG PUGINIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quảng trường Puginier is the earlier name for what became Ba Đình Square; the text notes the location’s openness and capacity for mass turnout."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quảng trường Puginier is the former name of Ba Đình Square, the site where the Tuyên ngôn Độc lập was read."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE FRENCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Free French (France libre) refers to the organizational affiliation of French officials like Jean Sainteny during the period surrounding Vietnam's decision-making and independence events."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LỄ THOÁI VỊ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lễ thoái vị is the abdication ceremony of Bao Đại, marking a pivotal political transition ahead of the independence process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dae09351baefd2c96da656733c534ccd</data>
    </node>
