    <edge source="&quot;CHĂM PA&quot;" target="&quot;ĐẠI VIỆT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">84.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Champa invasions occurred in the region and were resisted by Đại Việt in various campaigns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Changings in sovereignty: Champa became a vassal under Đại Việt in 1312, reflecting shifting regional power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312, marking a formal subordination; later Champa asserted independence and engaged in prolonged warfare to reclaim lands."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa became vassal of Đại Việt in 1312; later regained independence and waged a 30-year war to reclaim lands, against a backdrop of Tran dynasty decline."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa và Đế quốc Khmer liên quân tấn công Đại Việt ở các năm 1128 và 1132, nhằm quấy nhiễu nước ta."&lt;!-- Note: historical context --&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Đại Việt conducted campaigns against Champa (Chăm Pa) in the specified period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Đại Việt fought Champa in a protracted conflict to reclaim lands after Champa's period of independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312."|"political subordination"&lt;SEP&gt;"Đại Việt pursued reassertion of control during Cham incursions, including raids and attempts to recover territories."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa and Khmer attacked Đại Việt in the late 11th century."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa became a vassal (chư hầu) of Đại Việt as a result of marriages and alliances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chăm Pa became a vassal of Đại Việt in 1312, then regained independence about a decade later and waged a protracted war to reclaim lands."</data>
